window.HDH_SEARCH=[{"t":"Getting started","s":"","u":"docs/getting-started/","x":"!Animated walkthrough of three steps: index docs, connect the extension, scan a ticket. Gap Finder compares what customers ask in Zendesk tickets with your public documentation. It runs in two parts: this workspace ( Overview , Documentation , Extension ) and a Chrome or Edge extension that reads the open ticket."},{"t":"Getting started","s":"The three steps","u":"docs/getting-started/#the-three-steps","x":"1. Index your documentation. Open Documentation , enter your documentation homepage and press Index documentation . 2. Connect the extension. Open Extension , download and install it, then press Connect extension and type the code into the extension. 3. Scan a ticket. Open a Zendesk ticket, click the extension and press Scan ticket . The setup card on Overview tracks steps 1 and 2 and disappears when both are done. Select Show setup guide in the sidebar to bring it back. You can also use Documentation and Findings without an account: choose Continue without an account on the sign-in page. Loca"},{"t":"Indexing documentation","s":"","u":"docs/indexing/","x":"!A documentation address is entered and a progress bar fills until the article count appears."},{"t":"Indexing documentation","s":"Add a site","u":"docs/indexing/#add-a-site","x":"- Open Documentation , enter a Name for the source (for example, \"Example product public documentation\") and the Documentation URL of your public documentation, then press Add and index . - Wait for the progress text. The button shows Indexing… while it works. - When it finishes you see Documentation ready and the number of articles."},{"t":"Indexing documentation","s":"Name sources, add more and refresh","u":"docs/indexing/#name-sources-add-more-and-refresh","x":"- Each documentation site is a source with a name you choose. Click a name to rename it: press Enter to save or Esc to cancel. - Press + Add documentation source , enter a name and another address, then press Add and index . Articles from your other sources are kept. Only one source is indexed at a time, so wait for the progress text to finish first. - Press Refresh on a source to index it again. Its card shows the article count and when it was last indexed. - Sources indexed before names existed show their web address as the name until you rename them. - Only owners can add, rename, refresh o"},{"t":"Indexing documentation","s":"Limits and skipped pages","u":"docs/indexing/#limits-and-skipped-pages","x":"- Indexing is bounded. It stops at fixed page and size limits and only fetches public, safe addresses. - If the site is larger than the limits the status says Partial coverage . Some pages may be missing. - Linked pages that redirect or are not found are skipped and counted in the status. This is normally harmless."},{"t":"Indexing documentation","s":"Stop or continue","u":"docs/indexing/#stop-or-continue","x":"- Open Indexing options to Resume indexing after an interruption or Cancel indexing . - A cancelled or failed run leaves your earlier documentation unchanged."},{"t":"Indexing documentation","s":"Removing an indexed site","u":"docs/indexing/#removing-an-indexed-site","x":"- Open Documentation . Each source card has a Remove button (owners only). - Removing a source deletes its name and its indexed articles from the workspace. Other sites and articles you added by hand stay. You can index the site again later. - Saved findings keep their text but lose the link to the removed articles."},{"t":"Indexing documentation","s":"Cleaner articles","u":"docs/indexing/#cleaner-articles","x":"- Indexing drops menus, footers, cookie banners and sidebars, removes the site name from titles, keeps headings so they count more in matching, and skips duplicate articles (same title or same text), keeping the shortest address. - Articles you indexed earlier keep their old text. Press Refresh on each source to benefit."},{"t":"Connecting the extension","s":"","u":"docs/extension/","x":"!A one-time code appears in the workspace, is typed into the extension popup, and the popup shows Connected."},{"t":"Connecting the extension","s":"Install","u":"docs/extension/#install","x":"1. Open Extension and select Download extension . 2. Unzip the file. 3. Open chrome://extensions in Chrome or edge://extensions in Edge and turn on developer mode. 4. Choose Load unpacked and select the unzipped folder. 5. Pin the extension so it is one click away."},{"t":"Connecting the extension","s":"Connect","u":"docs/extension/#connect","x":"1. In Extension , press Connect extension . A six digit code appears with a countdown. 2. Open the extension popup and enter the code, then press Connect . 3. Allow the site permission when the browser asks. The workspace then shows Extension connected ."},{"t":"Connecting the extension","s":"Several devices","u":"docs/extension/#several-devices","x":"- Press Create 5 codes for several devices . Each code works once, on one browser, and expires on its own timer. - Use one code per browser or device."},{"t":"Connecting the extension","s":"Duration, disconnecting, revoking","u":"docs/extension/#duration-disconnecting-revoking","x":"- A connection lasts 30 days. Connect again when it ends. - To disconnect one browser, use the disconnect control in the extension popup. - To cut off every connection, open Manual pairing fallback on Extension and press Revoke my organization pairings ."},{"t":"Connecting the extension","s":"Update and check the version","u":"docs/extension/#update-and-check-the-version","x":"- To update, download the extension again, replace the folder and reload it on the extensions page. - Settings (the gear button) in the extension shows the version it is running."},{"t":"Connecting the extension","s":"Turning the extension on and off","u":"docs/extension/#turning-the-extension-on-and-off","x":"- Open Settings with the gear button at the top right of the extension popup. Extension on is the first switch there. When it is off, the extension does not read any ticket and Scan ticket is hidden. - Scan automatically when I open it is off by default. Leave it off to scan only when you press Scan ticket , or turn it on to scan the open ticket as soon as you open the extension. - The switches are remembered in your browser. Active browsers on Overview counts browsers that used the extension in the last 14 days, not every code that was ever entered."},{"t":"Connecting the extension","s":"Keeping documentation up to date","u":"docs/extension/#keeping-documentation-up-to-date","x":"- New or changed articles reach the extension on their own: it checks your access and refreshes its copy every time you press Scan ticket , and when it is older than 15 minutes if you scan automatically. - To refresh right away, open Settings in the extension and press Sync documentation now . It shows when it last synced. - The footer of the extension shows your source names. With one source it shows the name, the article count and the sync time. With several it shows the number of sources and lists each name with its count; press +N more to see them all. - When you have more than one source,"},{"t":"Scanning a ticket","s":"","u":"docs/scanning/","x":"!The ticket is read in the browser and matched against a local copy of the documentation. Nothing is sent out."},{"t":"Scanning a ticket","s":"How to scan","u":"docs/scanning/#how-to-scan","x":"1. Open a ticket in Zendesk and wait for it to load. 2. Click the extension. 3. Press Scan ticket ."},{"t":"Scanning a ticket","s":"What is matched","u":"docs/scanning/#what-is-matched","x":"- Only customer messages in the open ticket and its subject are matched. Agent replies and internal notes are not matched. Signatures, mail footers, quoted replies and phone or address lines are removed first, and later customer messages count a little more. - Only what is loaded on screen. If the conversation is long, scroll to load earlier messages and scan again. - Matching is deterministic text comparison against the documentation copy in your browser. No AI service is involved. !The three result groups: relevant documentation, potential gaps and suggested improvements."},{"t":"Scanning a ticket","s":"Reading the results","u":"docs/scanning/#reading-the-results","x":"- The coloured banner at the top is the verdict. It uses the same green, yellow, red and gray as the toolbar icon, with the number of relevant articles, potential gaps and articles checked. - In a narrow popup the lists become three tabs, Docs , Gaps and Ideas . Use the arrow keys to move between them. - Each article has Open article and Copy link . Select its passage to read more. - Relevant documentation lists articles whose words overlap with the question. - Potential gaps lists needs that have weak or no coverage. - Suggested improvements lists wording that could be added to an article. Ea"},{"t":"Scanning a ticket","s":"Short, non-English and billing tickets","u":"docs/scanning/#short-non-english-and-billing-tickets","x":"- Very short messages give little to match. Expect fewer or weaker results. - When a message repeats itself in two languages (for example French, a line, then English), the English part is analysed and the results say so. - Billing, account and cancellation questions are recognised and never produce gap suggestions. Feature requests show Looks like a feature request, not a documentation gap unless an article clearly matches. - The popup shows the detected ticket type under the ticket name, such as How-to question or Problem report . If a staff reply in the ticket links one of your indexed arti"},{"t":"How matching works","s":"","u":"docs/matching/","x":"!Words of the ticket are reduced to word stems, ranked against article text with title words counting more, and shown with the shared words. Matching is deterministic word comparison that runs in your browser. No AI, language model or paid service is involved, and the same ticket always gives the same result."},{"t":"How matching works","s":"What it does","u":"docs/matching/#what-it-does","x":"- Word forms: words are reduced to a stem, so install, installing and installation count as the same word, as do cache and caches. Words under four letters and words with digits are left alone. The chips still show the words as written. - Ranking: articles are ranked with the standard BM25 formula. Words in the title count three times, words in headings twice, and two neighbouring words found next to each other earn a small bonus. - Vocabulary: owners can list words that mean the same, such as slow, speed, performance and loading. A match through a synonym counts about 60% of an exact match. -"},{"t":"How matching works","s":"Vocabulary","u":"docs/matching/#vocabulary","x":"- Open Documentation and find the Vocabulary card. Type words separated by commas and press Add group . - A group has 2 to 12 words, letters only. A word can belong to one group only, and a workspace can have up to 200 groups. - Only owners change the list; members can read it. Browsers receive it with the other rules on their next sync, and it is never sent with a ticket."},{"t":"How matching works","s":"Limits","u":"docs/matching/#limits","x":"- A high score means shared wording, not a correct answer. Different wording without a synonym still looks like a gap. - Results are hedged on purpose. Treat every item as a lead to review."},{"t":"Status icon","s":"","u":"docs/status-icon/","x":"!Four toolbar icons with a small dot: green for docs found, yellow for partial or weak, red for a likely gap, gray for off or unknown. The extension can show the result of a ticket on its toolbar icon, so you see it without opening the popup. Turn on Show status on the toolbar icon in the popup and allow access to Zendesk when the browser asks."},{"t":"Status icon","s":"What the colours mean","u":"docs/status-icon/#what-the-colours-mean","x":"- Green (badge OK ): relevant documentation was found and no potential gap. - Yellow (badge ! ): documentation was found but there are potential gaps, or the matches are weak. - Red (badge GAP ): no relevant documentation and at least one potential gap. - Gray : off, not a ticket page, still scanning, no clear question found, a billing, account or cancellation request, a feature request, or the ticket could not be read. Hover over the icon to read the same result as text. A colour is a lead to review, not proof of a gap."},{"t":"Status icon","s":"Privacy","u":"docs/status-icon/#privacy","x":"- The scan runs in your browser on the ticket you have open. Ticket text is not stored and is not sent anywhere. - Turn the switch off at any time to clear every icon and badge. Extension on must also be on."},{"t":"Training the tool","s":"","u":"docs/training/","x":"!Agents mark potential gaps in the extension, the owner decides in Suggestions, and the decision returns to every connected browser. Agents can tell the tool when a potential gap is real or a false positive. The workspace owner reviews these in Suggestions , and the decisions change future scans in every connected browser."},{"t":"Training the tool","s":"For agents","u":"docs/training/#for-agents","x":"1. Scan a ticket in the extension. 2. Under Potential documentation gaps , read the line that starts with Sending . It lists the exact words that will be sent. 3. Press Real gap or Not a gap . The card then shows Sent ."},{"t":"Training the tool","s":"For the owner","u":"docs/training/#for-the-owner","x":"- Open Suggestions . Each card shows the key words, the closest article and how many people voted each way. - Approve as a gap moves it to Approved gaps , which you can export as CSV. - Dismiss as false positive hides matching gaps in the extension from the next scan. - An article covers this lets you pick an indexed article. Matching tickets then show that article under Relevant documentation . - Use Undo to reopen any decision."},{"t":"Training the tool","s":"Turning it off","u":"docs/training/#turning-it-off","x":"Owners can switch off Collect suggestions from the extension at the bottom of Suggestions . The extension then shows an error when someone presses a button. Reconnect or rescan to receive new decisions. The extension must be version 0.4.0 or later."},{"t":"Training the tool","s":"Deleting suggestions","u":"docs/training/#deleting-suggestions","x":"- Owners can press Delete on any suggestion, in any list. Deleting asks for confirmation. - Deleting a dismissed or covered suggestion also removes what the tool learned from it. - If agents report the same gap again later, it comes back as a new open suggestion."},{"t":"Training the tool","s":"Merged suggestions","u":"docs/training/#merged-suggestions","x":"- Suggestions with almost the same key words and the same closest article appear as one card, with Also reported as variants. Votes and distinct tickets are combined. - The list is ordered by distinct tickets, then distinct reporters, then recency. Open suggestions on the overview counts cards. - A decision on a card applies to every suggestion merged into it."},{"t":"Training the tool","s":"Learning from your team (owner opt-in)","u":"docs/training/#learning-from-your-team-owner-opt-in","x":"Two settings on Suggestions , both off by default and changed by owners only. Ticket text never leaves the browser. - Measure detection quality (counts only): when a staff reply links one of your indexed articles, the extension checks locally whether that article was in its top 3 and sends only whole numbers per day: tickets scanned, tickets with a linked article, top 1, top 3 and misses. Overview then shows Detection quality , for example the share of such tickets where the linked article was in the top 3. It measures how often matching finds the article your team chose, not whether a suggest"},{"t":"Findings and CSV import","s":"","u":"docs/findings/","x":"!A list of reviewed findings, each with a review state."},{"t":"Findings and CSV import","s":"Check a question here","u":"docs/findings/#check-a-question-here","x":"- Open Findings , enter a subject and the customer question and press Check documentation . - Set Review finding to Confirmed gap or Dismissed / covered . - Press Save current reviewed metadata to store the review in your workspace. The question text is not saved. - Export reviewed metadata downloads a CSV without the question or ticket content."},{"t":"Findings and CSV import","s":"Historical ticket CSV","u":"docs/findings/#historical-ticket-csv","x":"- Open Historical ticket CSV and choose a UTF-8 file, up to 20 MB and 100,000 rows. - Map the columns. ID, subject and description are required. - Press Import and redact . Emails and similar details are replaced before anything is shown. - Use Group and check imported tickets (up to 1,000) for a bulk check. Imported tickets live in the tab only."},{"t":"Team and permissions","s":"","u":"docs/team/","x":"!Three kinds of people in a workspace: owners, members and invited people. - Owners manage sources, members, invitations and Settings . - Members use the documentation they are allowed to see. - To invite someone, open Team , enter their Google account email and press Create invitation . No email is sent. Share the sign-in link yourself. Invitations expire after seven days. - Restricted sources are visible to owners and to members who were granted them. Save documentation only if you are authorized to share it. - Use New organization to create a separate workspace. The workspace switcher in th"},{"t":"Privacy and security","s":"","u":"docs/privacy/","x":"!Documentation flows into the browser. Ticket text never flows out to the server. - No AI. Matching, ticket types and ranking are fixed rules. Nothing readable is sent to any AI or third-party service. - Ticket text never leaves your browser. It is read, matched and discarded there. - Suggestions are the one exception, and only when you press a button. The extension sends a few filtered key words (lowercase letters only, no names, numbers, emails or links), a one-way fingerprint of them, the closest article and your vote. It also sends the ticket number and your Zendesk subdomain so a reviewer"},{"t":"Troubleshooting","s":"","u":"docs/troubleshooting/","x":"!Quick fixes for a rejected code, missing articles and empty results."},{"t":"Troubleshooting","s":"The code was rejected","u":"docs/troubleshooting/#the-code-was-rejected","x":"- Codes work once and expire. Press Connect extension for a new one and type it without delay. - Check you are in the same workspace you signed in to."},{"t":"Troubleshooting","s":"No articles after indexing","u":"docs/troubleshooting/#no-articles-after-indexing","x":"- Check the address opens without signing in. Only public pages are indexed. - Press Resume indexing , or index again and read the status text."},{"t":"Troubleshooting","s":"Nothing found for a ticket","u":"docs/troubleshooting/#nothing-found-for-a-ticket","x":"- Reload the documentation in the extension and scan again. - Short or non-English messages match less. See Scanning a ticket ."},{"t":"Troubleshooting","s":"The scan says to open a ticket","u":"docs/troubleshooting/#the-scan-says-to-open-a-ticket","x":"- Open a single ticket tab and wait until the conversation loads, then scan again."},{"t":"Troubleshooting","s":"The extension is out of date","u":"docs/troubleshooting/#the-extension-is-out-of-date","x":"- Download the extension again, replace the folder and reload it. Settings in the extension shows the version."},{"t":"Glossary and FAQ","s":"","u":"docs/glossary/","x":"!A match score bar: a hint of word overlap, not proof of coverage."},{"t":"Glossary and FAQ","s":"Glossary","u":"docs/glossary/#glossary","x":"- Indexing: reading your public documentation so it can be searched. - Source: a documentation site or document in your workspace. - Match score: a measure of word overlap between a ticket and an article. - Word stem: the shared core of word forms, so installing and installation match. - Vocabulary: owner-defined groups of words that mean the same. - Detection quality: how often the article a staff reply linked was in the extension's top 3 (counts only, opt-in). - Potential gap: a need with weak or no coverage that needs a human decision. - Reviewed metadata: the review state you save for a fi"},{"t":"Glossary and FAQ","s":"FAQ","u":"docs/glossary/#faq","x":"- Does it use AI? No. Matching is rule-based text retrieval. - Is ticket text uploaded? No. - Does it work offline? The app shell does. Indexing and account actions need a connection. - Can I use several workspaces? Yes. Use the workspace switcher in the top bar."}];